{
 "title": "When Demand Rises",
 "lang": "en",
 "steps": [
  {
   "title": "Set up axes",
   "say": "Let's draw a standard supply and demand graph, with Price on the vertical axis and Quantity on the horizontal axis.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "main_title",
     "x": 800,
     "y": 50,
     "text": "What Happens When Demand Rises?",
     "size": 48,
     "color": "ink",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "axis_p",
     "x1": 200,
     "y1": 700,
     "x2": 200,
     "y2": 180,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 4,
     "arrow": true
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "axis_q",
     "x1": 200,
     "y1": 700,
     "x2": 850,
     "y2": 700,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 4,
     "arrow": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_p",
     "x": 190,
     "y": 140,
     "text": "Price (P)",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "ink",
     "anchor": "middle"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_q",
     "x": 860,
     "y": 710,
     "text": "Quantity (Q)",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "ink",
     "anchor": "start"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Initial equilibrium",
   "say": "Here is our initial downward-sloping demand curve D1 and upward-sloping supply curve S. They cross at the first equilibrium, E1.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "curve_d1",
     "x1": 260,
     "y1": 260,
     "x2": 720,
     "y2": 660,
     "color": "blue",
     "width": 4
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_d1",
     "x": 730,
     "y": 660,
     "text": "D1",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "blue"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "curve_s",
     "x1": 260,
     "y1": 660,
     "x2": 720,
     "y2": 260,
     "color": "gray",
     "width": 4
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_s",
     "x": 730,
     "y": 240,
     "text": "S",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "gray"
    },
    {
     "op": "ellipse",
     "id": "pt_e1",
     "cx": 490,
     "cy": 460,
     "rx": 6,
     "ry": 6,
     "color": "ink",
     "fill": "ink"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_e1",
     "x": 510,
     "y": 445,
     "text": "E1",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Baseline price and quantity",
   "say": "At this intersection, the initial market-clearing price is P1, and the quantity sold is Q1.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "dash_p1",
     "x1": 490,
     "y1": 460,
     "x2": 200,
     "y2": 460,
     "color": "gray",
     "width": 2,
     "dash": true
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "dash_q1",
     "x1": 490,
     "y1": 460,
     "x2": 490,
     "y2": 700,
     "color": "gray",
     "width": 2,
     "dash": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_p1",
     "x": 160,
     "y": 442,
     "text": "P1",
     "size": 30,
     "color": "ink"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_q1",
     "x": 475,
     "y": 715,
     "text": "Q1",
     "size": 30,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Demand shifts right",
   "say": "When consumer demand increases, the entire demand curve shifts outward to the right, to D2.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "curve_d2",
     "x1": 400,
     "y1": 260,
     "x2": 820,
     "y2": 625,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 4
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_d2",
     "x": 830,
     "y": 625,
     "text": "D2",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "arrow_shift",
     "x1": 530,
     "y1": 340,
     "x2": 610,
     "y2": 340,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 3,
     "arrow": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "txt_shift",
     "x": 570,
     "y": 295,
     "text": "+ Demand",
     "size": 26,
     "color": "red",
     "anchor": "middle"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "New equilibrium",
   "say": "Along the stationary supply curve, the new crossing point moves up and to the right, to E2.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "ellipse",
     "id": "pt_e2",
     "cx": 610,
     "cy": 356,
     "rx": 6,
     "ry": 6,
     "color": "red",
     "fill": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_e2",
     "x": 625,
     "y": 335,
     "text": "E2",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "dash_p2",
     "x1": 610,
     "y1": 356,
     "x2": 200,
     "y2": 356,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 2,
     "dash": true
    },
    {
     "op": "line",
     "id": "dash_q2",
     "x1": 610,
     "y1": 356,
     "x2": 610,
     "y2": 700,
     "color": "red",
     "width": 2,
     "dash": true
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_p2",
     "x": 160,
     "y": 338,
     "text": "P2",
     "size": 30,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "lbl_q2",
     "x": 595,
     "y": 715,
     "text": "Q2",
     "size": 30,
     "color": "red"
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Conclusion",
   "say": "Buyers compete for limited supply, creating a shortage at the old price. Consequently, the equilibrium price rises, and quantity supplied increases.",
   "ops": [
    {
     "op": "rect",
     "id": "box_summary",
     "x": 980,
     "y": 240,
     "w": 540,
     "h": 420,
     "color": "ink",
     "width": 3,
     "fill": "gray"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sum_title",
     "x": 1020,
     "y": 275,
     "text": "Market Impact:",
     "size": 36,
     "color": "ink"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sum_p",
     "x": 1020,
     "y": 350,
     "text": "• Price rises  (P1 → P2)",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "red"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sum_q",
     "x": 1020,
     "y": 415,
     "text": "• Quantity rises  (Q1 → Q2)",
     "size": 32,
     "color": "green"
    },
    {
     "op": "write",
     "id": "sum_reason",
     "x": 1020,
     "y": 490,
     "text": "Why?\nHigher demand causes a shortage\nat P1, bidding prices up until\nsupply matches demand again.",
     "size": 28,
     "color": "ink"
    }
   ]
  }
 ]
}